WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.904
A negative belongs to a complete idea.

2
00:00:03.204 --> 00:00:08.153
Several negatives in one sentence still need to be handled one idea at a time.

3
00:00:08.453 --> 00:00:12.037
No proposal not approved for the trial is used in the trial.

4
00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:17.095
The excluded combination is not approved for this trial and used in this trial.

5
00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:21.811
First write not approved for the trial → not used in the trial.

6
00:00:22.111 --> 00:00:26.761
Its contrapositive says that use in the trial requires approval for the trial.

7
00:00:27.061 --> 00:00:29.216
The repeated trial restriction matters.

8
00:00:29.516 --> 00:00:32.375
Approval for some other purpose does not satisfy it.

9
00:00:32.675 --> 00:00:36.621
An answer can look simpler because it has quietly dropped a restriction.

10
00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:39.951
We want a shorter readable label, not a different rule.

11
00:00:40.251 --> 00:00:44.603
Write both complete conditions and the negative each actually contains.

12
00:00:44.903 --> 00:00:48.444
Apply the sentence’s relationship to those whole conditions.

13
00:00:48.744 --> 00:00:53.800
Keep the original sentence visible until the short labels have passed an English readback.

14
00:00:54.100 --> 00:01:00.969
Check negatives, subject and restriction separately; do not let getting one of them right conceal a change to another.
